<name>CAN Communication</name>
<ttl id="10033_S0007_741KB_T000K" variety="T000K">
<name>CAN Communication System</name>
<para id="RM000001LYP013X" category="C" type-id="801GF" name-id="9517F-01" from="200912">
<dtccode>U1002</dtccode>
<dtcname>Sub-network Communication Malfunction (CAN Gateway)</dtcname>
<subpara id="RM000001LYP013X_05" type-id="33" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CDH00001">
<name>Function Description</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<ptxt>The CAN gateway ECU outputs the code when it cannot receive data from any of the V bus No.2 connected ECUs whose connection is stored in memory.</ptxt>
<table pgwide="1">
<tgroup cols="3">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.42in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="2.34in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="3.32in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC No.</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Detection Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>DTC Output Related Items</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle" align="center">
<ptxt>U1002</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Data cannot be received from any of the ECUs whose connection is stored in the CAN gateway ECU memory</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>CAN V bus No.2 main line open or short circuit</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>V bus No.2 branch wire open or short circuit</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Poor connector terminal contact or contact pressure</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>CAN J/C internal short or open circuit</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>Network gateway computer (CAN gateway ECU) internal malfunction</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000001LYP013X_06" type-id="32" category="03" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CDI00001">
<name>Wiring Diagram</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="B249592J02" width="7.106578999in" height="5.787629434in"/>
</figure>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000001LYP013X_07" type-id="51" category="05" proc-id="RM0550J___0000CDJ00001">
<name>Inspection Procedure</name>
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When measuring the resistance of the CAN bus, turn the IG OFF, confirm that warning functions such as the key reminder warning system are not operating, and leave the vehicle for 1 minutes or more without operating the key or switches or opening/closing the doors before starting measurement. If it is necessary to open a door during inspection, open it beforehand.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>The following flowchart applies only when output by the CAN gateway ECU (V bus No.2 monitoring ECU). (If the main body ECU outputs U1002, refer to <xref label="Seep01" href="RM000002X34002X"/>)</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
<atten4>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>When inspecting each connector, before disconnecting it, push the connector case in the connecting direction and check that the connector is not loose or disconnected.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When disconnecting a connector, check that the connector terminals and connector case are free of damage, deformation, corrosion, etc.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten4>
</content5>
</subpara>
<subpara id="RM000001LYP013X_08" type-id="01" category="01">
